{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc | sed -n '1,670p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.remote\n     2\t  \"The UCF facade through `dao.stream.remote` descriptors: lifts a\n     3\t   parked semantic machine's pending wait\n     4\t   (`docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` S7.4.3) into\n     5\t   UCF data whose cells and stream markers name `dao.stream.remote`\n     6\t   descriptors under the `:dao.stream.remote/v1` cursor profile\n     7\t   (S7.5.3), and lowers that data back into a resumable local wait\n     8\t   through a reflection (`docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md` S2.2,\n     9\t   S2.4).\n    10\t\n    11\t   The local side is the engine's own parked machinery, not an\n    12\t   invented shape. A pending entry is what `yin.vm` parks: the\n    13\t   machine registers beside `:stream-id` and `:cursor-ref`\n    14\t   (`yin.vm.semantic` S3.5's park entries, `response-wait-entry`;\n    15\t   `yin.vm.engine`'s wait-set sweep), every handle and cursor\n    16\t   resolved out of the machine's private `:resources` table -- the\n    17\t   lift reads the table, and no entry ever carries a live handle.\n    18\t   The lower mirrors it: fresh resource entries, one per stream\n    19\t   reflection and one per cursor cell (two waiters sharing one cell\n    20\t   share the one entry, S7.5.3), and wait-set entries that merge the\n    21\t   caller's register context verbatim, so a lowered wait parks under\n    22\t   the engine's own sweep exactly as an unmigrated one does.\n    23\t\n    24\t   Where the engine polls a wait at one of its own fixed resource\n    25\t   keys, the lower parks the wait there: a link wait's pair under\n    26\t   `yin.vm.module`'s link-request-resource and\n    27\t   link-response-resource, reflections and entry fields alike, and a\n    28\t   retained request as the engine's own `:request-sent` shape on the\n    29\t   fixed local call-in key -- the receiver's own pair serves the\n    30\t   retried request and the restored response wait reads the\n    31\t   receiver's own call-out, so the fixed keys serve the resumed\n    32\t   program's calls alone. Every response route travels as its cell\n    33\t   and lowers under the cell's own fresh key (S7.5.3) -- distinct\n    34\t   cells stay distinct, shared cells stay shared -- never at a fixed\n    35\t   key, so a migrated route can never misroute a new call.\n    36\t\n    37\t   `lift-pending` and `lower-pending` are plain-data functions,\n    38\t   parameterized by two composition callbacks rather than coupled to\n    39\t   `yin.vm` or `dao.stream.remote` internals:\n    40\t\n    41\t     serve!  : handle -> {:dao.stream/identity id\n    42\t                          :dao.stream/channel chan} | nil\n    43\t               the exporter's own table entry\n    44\t               (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.3): nil when the handle\n    45\t               cannot be served -- no table to enter it in, no\n    46\t               channel to the resumer -- which refuses the lift as\n    47\t               `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before minting the value\n    48\t               (S7.4.3).\n    49\t\n    50\t     attach! : remote-descriptor -> {:dao.stream/outcome\n    51\t                                     :dao.stream/ok\n    52\t                                     :dao.stream/handle reflection}\n    53\t               | outcome-map\n    54\t               the receiver's own `:dao.stream/attach` dispatch for\n    55\t               `:dao.stream/remote` (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.4): an\n    56\t               outcome other than `ok` -- including a reflection\n    57\t               already marked gone -- refuses the lower as\n    58\t               `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the stream identity.\n    59\t\n    60\t   The `:dao.stream.remote/v1` claim is checked, not declared: a cell\n    61\t   is published only after its kept cursor survives a round trip\n    62\t   through the channel codec -- encoded, decoded back, equal -- which\n    63\t   is what plain data in the channel's portable domain means\n    64\t   (S7.4.3; `dao.stream.remote.md` S2.3's plain-data basis).\n    65\t   `cursor-codec` is the default codec; a composition whose channel\n    66\t   speaks another passes its own `{:encode f :decode f}` to\n    67\t   `lift-pending` or `lift-frame`. A cursor that does not round trip\n    68\t   -- a host object inside is the case S2.3 names -- refuses the lift\n    69\t   as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before any value is minted.\n    70\t\n    71\t   Every pending variant of S7.4.3 lifts and lowers: `:next`, `:put`,\n    72\t   `:ffi`, `:ffi-request`, and the linker's `:link-request`,\n    73\t   `:link-response` and `:install` (`yin.vm.linker.md` S7.2-7.3).\n    74\t   `:install` names no stream and passes through unchanged.\n    75\t\n    76\t   Scope: `lift-frame` and `lower-frame` are the frame-level entry\n    77\t   points -- cells are minted and remapped across the WHOLE entry\n    78\t   set, so two waiters on one engine cursor cell lift to one UCF\n    79\t   cell and lower back into one shared cursor entry, and independent\n    80\t   cells stay independent (S7.5.3, and the sharing rule of the S7.11\n    81\t   pending-state blocker). `lift-pending` and `lower-pending` lift or\n    82\t   lower one entry into a self-contained table.\"\n    83\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n    84\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n    85\t            [dao.stream.cbor :as cbor]\n    86\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    87\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(def cursor-profiles\n    91\t  \"The one portable cursor profile S7.4.3 names in :yin.k/requires: a\n    92\t   cursor is plain data in the channel's portable domain and the\n    93\t   source honors it after serialization, cursor identity, position and\n    94\t   `gap` outcomes included.\"\n    95\t  #{:dao.stream.remote/v1})\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t(def cursor-codec\n    99\t  \"The channel codec a lift round-trips kept cursors through when the\n   100\t   composition supplies none: the DaoStream v2 wire codec, whose\n   101\t   portable domain is the domain the profile claim names.\"\n   102\t  {:encode cbor/encode, :decode cbor/decode})\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\t(def ^:private requires\n   106\t  {:yin.k/cursor-profiles cursor-profiles})\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\t;; =============================================================================\n   110\t;; Markers (S7.5.1), through a remote descriptor\n   111\t;; =============================================================================\n   112\t\n   113\t(defn- local-identity\n   114\t  \"The identity `h` itself declares, when its descriptor answers ok;\n   115\t   nil otherwise -- the best name a refusal can give when `serve!` has\n   116\t   not minted one.\"\n   117\t  [h]\n   118\t  (let [d (when (stream/descriptor? h) (stream/descriptor h))]\n   119\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome d))\n   120\t      (:dao.stream/identity d))))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- unsatisfied\n   124\t  ([] (unsatisfied nil))\n   125\t  ([identity]\n   126\t   (cond-> {:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied}\n   127\t     (some? identity) (assoc :dao.stream/identity identity))))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn- portable-cursor\n   131\t  \"The kept cursor when it survives a round trip through the channel\n   132\t   codec -- encoded, decoded back, and equal -- which is what the\n   133\t   `:dao.stream.remote/v1` claim means: plain data in the channel's\n   134\t   portable domain, honored after serialization. nil when it does\n   135\t   not, so no cell is ever published over an unpublishable cursor.\"\n   136\t  [codec cursor]\n   137\t  (try (let [w (:encode codec)\n   138\t             b (w cursor)\n   139\t             r ((:decode codec) b)]\n   140\t         (when (= cursor r) cursor))\n   141\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n   142\t\n   143\t\n   144\t(defn lift-marker\n   145\t  \"The UCF stream marker (S7.5.1) for local handle `h`, its descriptor\n   146\t   the remote descriptor `serve!` mints by entering `h` in the\n   147\t   exporter's table (`dao.stream.remote.md` S2.2). nil when `serve!`\n   148\t   refuses -- the source cannot be entered, or cannot honor the\n   149\t   profile -- so a caller mints `:yin.k/unsatisfied` before any value\n   150\t   is produced (S7.4.3).\"\n   151\t  [serve! h]\n   152\t  (when-let [served (serve! h)]\n   153\t    (let [id (:dao.stream/identity served)]\n   154\t      {:yin.k/tag :yin.k/stream,\n   155\t       :dao.stream/identity id,\n   156\t       :dao.stream/descriptor\n   157\t       {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote,\n   158\t        :dao.stream/identity id,\n   159\t        :dao.stream/channel (:dao.stream/channel served)}})))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(defn lower-marker\n   163\t  \"The local handle `attach!` gives for UCF stream marker `m` -- a\n   164\t   reflection on the original logical stream -- or nil when the attach\n   165\t   does not answer ok: a reflection marked gone, or any other refusal,\n   166\t   is unsatisfied at the caller.\"\n   167\t  [attach! m]\n   168\t  (let [result (attach! (:dao.stream/descriptor m))]\n   169\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n   170\t      (:dao.stream/handle result))))\n   171\t\n   172\t\n   173\t;; =============================================================================\n   174\t;; The pending wait (S7.4.3)\n   175\t;; =============================================================================\n   176\t;;\n   177\t;; Local pending-entry shapes this namespace lifts, and lowers back to\n   178\t;; -- the engine's own wait-set shapes, plain data resolved through\n   179\t;; the machine's `:resources` table:\n   180\t;;\n   181\t;;   {:reason :next          :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid}\n   182\t;;                           :stream-id sid}          ; blocked read\n   183\t;;   {:reason :next          :call-id id :op op        ; a sent call's\n   184\t;;                           :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid}\n   185\t;;                           :stream-id sid}          ; response wait\n   186\t;;   {:reason :put           :stream-id sid            ; blocked write,\n   187\t;;                           :datom v}                 ; :datom the retry\n   188\t;;   {:reason :put           :request-sent true        ; a retained FFI\n   189\t;;                           :call-id id :op op        ; request; the\n   190\t;;                           :stream-id sid :datom env}; fixed call-in\n   191\t;;   {:reason :link-request  :link-id id :name m :envelope e\n   192\t;;                           :request rid :response rid' :cursor kept}\n   193\t;;   {:reason :link-response :link-id id :name m\n   194\t;;                           :request rid :response rid' :cursor kept}\n   195\t;;   {:reason :install       :name m}\n   196\t;;\n   197\t;; `cid` names a `:resources` cursor entry `{:stream-id sid :cursor\n   198\t;; kept}` (`vm/cursor-entry`); `sid` and `rid` name stream handles in\n   199\t;; the same table; `env` is the retained `dao.stream.apply` envelope.\n   200\t;; On a real entry the retained request's `sid` is the engine's fixed\n   201\t;; `vm/call-in-stream-key`, and a link wait's `rid`/`rid'` are the\n   202\t;; fixed `module/link-request-resource` and\n   203\t;; `module/link-response-resource` -- the keys the engine's own retry\n   204\t;; and poll paths resolve.\n   205\t;; The registers every parked entry also carries -- :segment :pc :env\n   206\t;; :stack :k -- are the machine's own context: the lift ignores them\n   207\t;; (they travel in the frame's continuation slice, not the pending\n   208\t;; wait), and the lower stamps the caller's context back onto the\n   209\t;; entry it builds.\n   210\t\n   211\t\n   212\t;; =============================================================================\n   213\t;; Cell minting and remapping (S7.5.3), across the whole frame set\n   214\t;; =============================================================================\n   215\t\n   216\t(defn- mint-cell\n   217\t  \"One mint per distinct cursor cell across the WHOLE frame set:\n   218\t   `found` accumulates the remapping {cell key -> UCF cell id} beside\n   219\t   the cells themselves as entries lift, so two waiters on one\n   220\t   engine cursor cell lift to one UCF cell, and independent cells\n   221\t   stay independent, whatever their positions (S7.5.3). `k` is the\n   222\t   cell's identity -- the engine cursor resource id a `:next` waiter\n   223\t   names, or the response stream and kept cursor a link wait names.\n   224\t   The cell carries the marker `serve!` mints for the cell's stream\n   225\t   and its kept cursor, published only after the cursor survives the\n   226\t   codec round trip; nil -- refuse -- when it does not, or when\n   227\t   `serve!` refuses the stream.\"\n   228\t  [serve! found]\n   229\t  (fn [codec k handle kept]\n   230\t    (or (get-in @found [:of k])\n   231\t        (let [portable (portable-cursor codec kept)\n   232\t              marker (when portable (lift-marker serve! handle))]\n   233\t          (when (and portable marker)\n   234\t            (let [cid (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"c-\" (count (:cells @found))))\n   235\t                  cell {:yin.k/stream marker, :yin.k/position portable}]\n   236\t              (swap! found #(-> % (assoc-in [:of k] cid)\n   237\t                                (assoc-in [:cells cid] cell)))\n   238\t              cid))))))\n   239\t\n   240\t\n   241\t(defn- cursor-cell\n   242\t  \"The engine cursor cell a `:next` entry waits on: `:cursor-ref`'s\n   243\t   id into `:resources`, the cursor entry carrying the stream id and\n   244\t   the kept cursor (`vm/cursor-entry`). nil when it names nothing.\"\n   245\t  [resources entry]\n   246\t  (let [cid (get-in entry [:cursor-ref :id])\n   247\t        cell (get resources cid)]\n   248\t    (when (and (some? cid) (map? cell) (contains? cell :stream-id))\n   249\t      {:id cid, :stream-id (:stream-id cell), :cursor (:cursor cell)})))\n   250\t\n   251\t\n   252\t(defn- cell-identity\n   253\t  \"The stream identity a `:yin.k/cells` entry names, for a refusal\n   254\t   that names it even when the cell itself never lowered.\"\n   255\t  [cells cell-id]\n   256\t  (get-in cells [cell-id :yin.k/stream :dao.stream/identity]))\n   257\t\n   258\t\n   259\t;; =============================================================================\n   260\t;; Lift: one variant each\n   261\t;; =============================================================================\n   262\t\n   263\t(defn- lift-read\n   264\t  \"S7.4.3's blocked read: the cell `mint` gives for the entry's\n   265\t   cursor cell, at its kept position.\"\n   266\t  [resources mint codec entry]\n   267\t  (if-let [cell (cursor-cell resources entry)]\n   268\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec (:id cell)\n   269\t                       (get resources (:stream-id cell))\n   270\t                       (:cursor cell))]\n   271\t      {:pending {:yin.k/reason :next, :yin.k/cell cid}, :cell? true}\n   272\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity (get resources (:stream-id cell)))))\n   273\t    (unsatisfied)))\n   274\t\n   275\t\n   276\t(defn- lift-response-wait\n   277\t  \"S7.4.3's sent call: a `:next` entry carrying `:call-id`, the\n   278\t   response wait `semantic-restore` rebuilds -- the call's\n   279\t   correlation beside the response cell at its kept position, so\n   280\t   round-order on the cell is preserved on the resumer (S7.4.3).\n   281\t   The call's `:op` rides when the entry carries it (the engine's\n   282\t   own response wait does not; a caller assembling the frame takes\n   283\t   it from the call's parked record).\"\n   284\t  [resources mint codec entry]\n   285\t  (if-let [cell (cursor-cell resources entry)]\n   286\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec (:id cell)\n   287\t                       (get resources (:stream-id cell))\n   288\t                       (:cursor cell))]\n   289\t      {:pending (cond-> {:yin.k/reason :ffi,\n   290\t                         :yin.k/call-id (:call-id entry),\n   291\t                         :yin.k/cell cid}\n   292\t                  (contains? entry :op) (assoc :yin.k/op (:op entry))),\n   293\t       :cell? true}\n   294\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity (get resources (:stream-id cell)))))\n   295\t    (unsatisfied)))\n   296\t\n   297\t\n   298\t(defn- lift-write\n   299\t  \"S7.4.3's blocked write: the target stream's marker and the\n   300\t   retained `:datom` -- the value a retry appends, without which the\n   301\t   wait is not re-establishable. A put names a stream, never a\n   302\t   cursor cell.\"\n   303\t  [serve! resources entry]\n   304\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))]\n   305\t    (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\n   306\t      {:pending {:yin.k/reason :put,\n   307\t                 :yin.k/stream marker,\n   308\t                 :yin.k/value (:datom entry)}}\n   309\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))))\n   310\t\n   311\t\n   312\t(defn- call-out-cell\n   313\t  \"The emitter's call-out cursor cell -- the response route the\n   314\t   retained call had on the emitter: the cursor entry under\n   315\t   `vm/call-out-cursor-key`, reading the call-out stream under\n   316\t   `vm/call-out-stream-key` at its kept position. nil when the\n   317\t   composition holds no call pair, which no real retained request\n   318\t   does -- the pair is checked before the call parked.\"\n   319\t  [resources]\n   320\t  (let [cursor (get resources vm/call-out-cursor-key)\n   321\t        handle (get resources vm/call-out-stream-key)]\n   322\t    (when (and (map? cursor) (contains? cursor :stream-id) handle)\n   323\t      {:id vm/call-out-cursor-key,\n   324\t       :stream-id vm/call-out-stream-key,\n   325\t       :cursor (:cursor cursor)})))\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\t(defn- lift-retained-request\n   329\t  \"S7.4.3's retained call: a `:put` entry carrying `:request-sent`,\n   330\t   the request the engine holds unsent. Both endpoints are served --\n   331\t   the request stream's marker and the response stream's marker,\n   332\t   `call-out-cell`'s -- and the retained envelope is read out\n   333\t   verbatim (`:request-op`, `:request-args`) beside the kept\n   334\t   response cell (`:yin.k/response-cell`), so a resumer can\n   335\t   re-establish the carried pair: retry through the request\n   336\t   reflection, wait for the response through the response reflection\n   337\t   at the kept position. Either endpoint unservable refuses as\n   338\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming that endpoint's identity, before any\n   339\t   value is minted.\"\n   340\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   341\t  (let [h (get resources (:stream-id entry))\n   342\t        envelope (:datom entry)\n   343\t        route (call-out-cell resources)\n   344\t        resp-h (and route (get resources (:stream-id route)))]\n   345\t    (if-let [marker (lift-marker serve! h)]\n   346\t      (if-let [resp-marker (and resp-h (lift-marker serve! resp-h))]\n   347\t        (if-let [cid (mint codec (:id route) resp-h (:cursor route))]\n   348\t          {:pending {:yin.k/reason :ffi-request,\n   349\t                     :yin.k/call-id (:call-id entry),\n   350\t                     :yin.k/request-op (or (apply2/request-op envelope)\n   351\t                                           (:op entry)),\n   352\t                     :yin.k/request-args (apply2/request-args envelope),\n   353\t                     :yin.k/request marker,\n   354\t                     :yin.k/response resp-marker,\n   355\t                     :yin.k/response-cell cid},\n   356\t           :cell? true}\n   357\t          (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))\n   358\t        (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))\n   359\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity h)))))\n   360\t\n   361\t\n   362\t(defn- lift-link\n   363\t  \"S7.4.3's link variants: the link pair name the engine's own fixed\n   364\t   link keys on a real entry (`module/link-request-resource` and\n   365\t   `module/link-response-resource`), resolved into `:resources`, and\n   366\t   the kept `:cursor` on the response stream\n   367\t   (`module/require-handler` mints it before the envelope is appended)\n   368\t   is the response cell -- a cell like any other, at its kept\n   369\t   position. Both pair markers travel, the engine's `:link-response`\n   370\t   entry retaining its `:request` beside the response side; the\n   371\t   envelope rides verbatim on the request-in-hand variant.\"\n   372\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   373\t  (let [reason (:reason entry)\n   374\t        resp-h (get resources (:response entry))\n   375\t        req-h (get resources (:request entry))\n   376\t        kept (:cursor entry)]\n   377\t    (if-let [cid (mint codec [(:response entry) kept] resp-h kept)]\n   378\t      (let [resp (lift-marker serve! resp-h)\n   379\t            req (lift-marker serve! req-h)]\n   380\t        (if (and resp req)\n   381\t          {:pending (cond-> {:yin.k/reason reason,\n   382\t                             :yin.k/link-id (:link-id entry),\n   383\t                             :yin.k/name (:name entry),\n   384\t                             :yin.k/request req,\n   385\t                             :yin.k/response resp,\n   386\t                             :yin.k/cell cid}\n   387\t                      (= :link-request reason)\n   388\t                      (assoc :yin.k/envelope (:envelope entry))),\n   389\t           :cell? true}\n   390\t          (unsatisfied (local-identity (or req-h resp-h)))))\n   391\t      (unsatisfied (local-identity resp-h)))))\n   392\t\n   393\t\n   394\t(defn- lift-one\n   395\t  \"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lifted into `{:pending data,\n   396\t   :cell? bool}` -- `:cell?` true when the variant names a cursor\n   397\t   cell, which is what puts `:dao.stream.remote/v1` in\n   398\t   `:yin.k/cursor-profiles` -- or an outcome carrying\n   399\t   `:yin.k/status`: `:yin.k/unsatisfied` when a stream cannot be\n   400\t   served or a kept cursor does not survive the codec round trip;\n   401\t   `:yin.k/undecodable`, naming the reason, when the entry is no\n   402\t   variant at all.\"\n   403\t  [serve! resources mint codec entry]\n   404\t  (case (:reason entry)\n   405\t    :next\n   406\t    (if (:call-id entry)\n   407\t      (lift-response-wait resources mint codec entry)\n   408\t      (lift-read resources mint codec entry))\n   409\t\n   410\t    :put\n   411\t    (if (:request-sent entry)\n   412\t      (lift-retained-request serve! resources mint codec entry)\n   413\t      (lift-write serve! resources entry))\n   414\t\n   415\t    :link-request (lift-link serve! resources mint codec entry)\n   416\t\n   417\t    :link-response (lift-link serve! resources mint codec entry)\n   418\t\n   419\t    :install\n   420\t    {:pending {:yin.k/reason :install, :yin.k/name (:name entry)}}\n   421\t\n   422\t    {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable, :yin.k/reason (:reason entry)}))\n   423\t\n   424\t\n   425\t;; =============================================================================\n   426\t;; Lift: the frame and the single entry\n   427\t;; =============================================================================\n   428\t\n   429\t(defn lift-frame\n   430\t  \"A whole frame set of S7.4.3 pending entries, lifted together:\n   431\t   `{:yin.k/pending [data ...], :yin.k/cells {cell-id cell},\n   432\t   :yin.k/requires requires}` on success -- the cells minted across\n   433\t   the WHOLE set, so two waiters on one engine cursor cell lift to\n   434\t   one UCF cell (S7.5.3) and `:dao.stream.remote/v1` rides in\n   435\t   `:yin.k/cursor-profiles` when any entry names a cell; the S7.9\n   436\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` outcome, naming the stream identity where one\n   437\t   is known, when any entry's stream cannot be served or its kept\n   438\t   cursor does not survive the codec round trip; the S7.9\n   439\t   `:yin.k/undecodable` outcome when any entry names no variant.\n   440\t   Failure is total (S7.5.4): a refused leaf refuses the frame.\"\n   441\t  ([serve! resources entries]\n   442\t   (lift-frame serve! resources entries cursor-codec))\n   443\t  ([serve! resources entries codec]\n   444\t   (let [found (atom {:cells {}, :of {}})\n   445\t         mint (mint-cell serve! found)\n   446\t         lifted (mapv #(lift-one serve! resources mint codec %) entries)]\n   447\t     (if-let [refusal (some #(when (contains? % :yin.k/status) %) lifted)]\n   448\t       refusal\n   449\t       {:yin.k/pending (mapv :pending lifted),\n   450\t        :yin.k/cells (:cells @found),\n   451\t        :yin.k/requires (if (some :cell? lifted) requires {})}))))\n   452\t\n   453\t\n   454\t(defn lift-pending\n   455\t  \"One pending entry of S7.4.3, lifted into its own self-contained\n   456\t   cell table: `{:yin.k/pending data, :yin.k/cells {cell-id cell},\n   457\t   :yin.k/requires requires}` on success, with the same `:yin.k/\n   458\t   unsatisfied` and `:yin.k/undecodable` outcomes `lift-frame`\n   459\t   gives. Frame assembly that shares cells across entries is\n   460\t   `lift-frame`'s.\"\n   461\t  ([serve! resources entry]\n   462\t   (lift-pending serve! resources entry cursor-codec))\n   463\t  ([serve! resources entry codec]\n   464\t   (let [r (lift-frame serve! resources [entry] codec)]\n   465\t     (if (contains? r :yin.k/status)\n   466\t       r\n   467\t       (assoc r :yin.k/pending (first (:yin.k/pending r)))))))\n   468\t\n   469\t\n   470\t;; =============================================================================\n   471\t;; Lower: back into resources and a wait-set entry\n   472\t;; =============================================================================\n   473\t\n   474\t(def ^:private fixed-resource-keys\n   475\t  \"The VM's fixed private resource keys -- the FFI call pair and the\n   476\t   link pair. Batch-allocated keys never collide with them, and the\n   477\t   lower installs nothing at them but what the engine's own dispatch\n   478\t   reads there: the link pair, and a retained request's fixed local\n   479\t   call-in key.\"\n   480\t  #{vm/call-in-stream-key vm/call-out-stream-key\n   481\t    vm/call-out-cursor-key module/link-request-resource\n   482\t    module/link-response-resource})\n   483\t\n   484\t\n   485\t(defn- fresh-key\n   486\t  \"The next private resource key `used` does not hold, claiming it:\n   487\t   `:yin.k/k-1`, `:yin.k/k-2`, ... regenerating on any collision\n   488\t   with the receiver's existing resources, the VM's fixed keys, or\n   489\t   keys this batch already allocated.\"\n   490\t  [used]\n   491\t  (loop [n (inc (count @used))]\n   492\t    (let [k (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"k-\" n))]\n   493\t      (if (contains? @used k)\n   494\t        (recur (inc n))\n   495\t        (do (swap! used conj k) k)))))\n   496\t\n   497\t\n   498\t(defn- pending-markers\n   499\t  \"Every stream marker `pending` names beside its cells' -- the\n   500\t   target of a put, both endpoints of a retained call, the pair of\n   501\t   a link request.\"\n   502\t  [pending]\n   503\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   504\t    :put [(:yin.k/stream pending)]\n   505\t    :ffi-request [(:yin.k/request pending)\n   506\t                  (:yin.k/response pending)]\n   507\t    (:link-request :link-response)\n   508\t    [(:yin.k/request pending)\n   509\t     (:yin.k/response pending)]\n   510\t    []))\n   511\t\n   512\t\n   513\t(defn- attach-all\n   514\t  \"One attach per distinct stream identity. The first attach that\n   515\t   does not answer ok -- a reflection marked gone included -- refuses\n   516\t   the lower as `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming that identity. Returns\n   517\t   {:handles {identity handle}}; `lower-frame` allocates each\n   518\t   reflection its own collision-free resource key.\"\n   519\t  [attach! markers]\n   520\t  (let [by-id (reduce (fn [m mkr]\n   521\t                        (update m (:dao.stream/identity mkr) #(or % mkr)))\n   522\t                      {} markers)]\n   523\t    (reduce-kv (fn [acc identity mkr]\n   524\t                 (if-let [h (lower-marker attach! mkr)]\n   525\t                   (assoc-in acc [:handles identity] h)\n   526\t                   (reduced (unsatisfied identity))))\n   527\t               {:handles {}}\n   528\t               by-id)))\n   529\t\n   530\t\n   531\t(defn- cell-resources\n   532\t  \"The fresh cursor entry each UCF cell lowers to, under the key\n   533\t   `cell-keys` allocated for it: its carried position, on the\n   534\t   reflection of the stream the cell names. Two references to one\n   535\t   cell share the one entry, and one ref per cell keeps its own\n   536\t   (S7.5.3); equal cell ids across separately lowered frames got\n   537\t   different keys, so no two frames ever share an entry. A response\n   538\t   route is no exception: it lowers under its own fresh key, never\n   539\t   at a fixed key, so distinct routes stay distinct and no migrated\n   540\t   route can ever misroute a new call.\"\n   541\t  [streams cells cell-keys]\n   542\t  (into {}\n   543\t        (map (fn [[cid cell]]\n   544\t               [(cell-keys cid)\n   545\t                {:stream-id (streams (cell-identity cells cid)),\n   546\t                 :cursor (:yin.k/position cell)}]))\n   547\t        cells))\n   548\t\n   549\t\n   550\t(defn- link-pair-resources\n   551\t  \"The engine's fixed link keys (`module/link-request-resource`,\n   552\t   `module/link-response-resource`) mapped onto the reflections a\n   553\t   lowered link wait uses: the engine's sweep retries a\n   554\t   `:link-request` by appending at the fixed request key\n   555\t   (`module/append-link-request`) and polls a `:link-response` at the\n   556\t   fixed response key (`poll-link-response`), so a lowered link wait\n   557\t   parks where the engine looks. One pair per task: the identity of\n   558\t   each side rides the pending's own markers.\"\n   559\t  [streams resources pendings]\n   560\t  (reduce (fn [acc pending]\n   561\t            (if (contains? #{:link-request :link-response}\n   562\t                           (:yin.k/reason pending))\n   563\t              (let [req-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   564\t                                            :dao.stream/identity])\n   565\t                    resp-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/response\n   566\t                                             :dao.stream/identity])\n   567\t                    req (get resources (streams req-id))\n   568\t                    resp (get resources (streams resp-id))]\n   569\t                (if (and req resp)\n   570\t                  (assoc acc\n   571\t                         module/link-request-resource req,\n   572\t                         module/link-response-resource resp)\n   573\t                  acc))\n   574\t              acc))\n   575\t          {}\n   576\t          pendings))\n   577\t\n   578\t\n   579\t(defn- lower-one\n   580\t  \"One pending of S7.4.3, lowered: `{:entry e}` -- the wait-set\n   581\t   entry the receiver parks, the caller's register context `ctx`\n   582\t   merged verbatim under the stream and cell fields the data\n   583\t   rebuilds -- or an outcome carrying `:yin.k/status`, naming the\n   584\t   stream identity where one is known. Every wait polls the key\n   585\t   `cell-keys` allocated for its cell, reading the stream key\n   586\t   `streams` allocated for the cell's reflection: migrated waits\n   587\t   poll routes no new call shares. A retained request's retry\n   588\t   writes through the request reflection's allocated key and stamps\n   589\t   the carried response route (`:response-cursor`,\n   590\t   `:response-stream`) for its restore.\"\n   591\t  [pending ctx streams cells cell-keys]\n   592\t  (case (:yin.k/reason pending)\n   593\t    :next\n   594\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)]\n   595\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\n   596\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   597\t                       {:reason :next,\n   598\t                        :stream-id sid,\n   599\t                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref,\n   600\t                                     :id (cell-keys cid)}})}\n   601\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\n   602\t\n   603\t    :put\n   604\t    (if-let [sid (streams (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream\n   605\t                                           :dao.stream/identity]))]\n   606\t      {:entry (merge ctx\n   607\t                     {:reason :put,\n   608\t                      :stream-id sid,\n   609\t                      :datom (:yin.k/value pending)})}\n   610\t      (unsatisfied (get-in pending [:yin.k/stream :dao.stream/identity])))\n   611\t\n   612\t    :ffi\n   613\t    (let [cid (:yin.k/cell pending)]\n   614\t      (if-let [sid (streams (cell-identity cells cid))]\n   615\t        {:entry (merge ctx\n   616\t                       (cond-> {:reason :next,\n   617\t                                :call-id (:yin.k/call-id pending),\n   618\t                                :stream-id sid,\n   619\t                                :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref,\n   620\t                                             :id (cell-keys cid)}}\n   621\t                         (contains? pending :yin.k/op)\n   622\t                         (assoc :op (:yin.k/op pending))))}\n   623\t        (unsatisfied (cell-identity cells cid))))\n   624\t\n   625\t    :ffi-request\n   626\t    (let [req-id (get-in pending [:yin.k/request\n   627\t                                  :dao.stream/ident