{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1790530211570-vm-engineer-dao-stream-remote-slice8-fixes-r4.glm-flash.report.md'","aggregated_output":"The structural fix (gate r5).** Every fixed-key route installation is gone; cells lower under their own fresh keys, and the receiver's fixed keys serve only the receiver's own pair:\n\n- **(1)+(3) Route cells lower under their own cell ids.** `cell-resources` is uniform again — every UCF cell lowers to `{:stream-id <fresh reflection key>, :cursor kept}` under the cell id itself, a response route included (src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:522-535). `route-cells` and `cursor-entry-key` are deleted, and with them the `vm/call-out-cursor-key` installation — the only remaining reference to that key in the lower is the LIFT-side emitter resolver `call-out-cell` (remote.cljc:315-326), which reads the emitter's table. Distinct cells get distinct keys; co-waiters sharing a cell share it — §7.5.3 both ways, and the multi-cell overwrite is structurally impossible.\n- **(2) Lowered waits' refs name the fresh key.** `:next` and `:ffi` waits build `:cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref, :id cid}` (the cell's fresh key) with `:stream-id` = the cell stream's fresh reflection key (remote.cljc:583, :602) — migrated waits poll routes no new call shares (engine.cljc:522 resolves the stream from the cursor cell, so the refs are data, exactly as the gate stated).\n- **The retained call keeps the engine's own shape, retry-local.** `:ffi-request` lowers as `{:reason :put, :request-sent true, :stream-id vm/call-in-stream-key, :datom <envelope rebuilt verbatim>}` (remote.cljc:610-621) — the engine's own retained shape (semantic.cljc:458-473) — so the receiver's own bridge serves the retried request, the response lands on the receiver's own call-out, and the restored response wait (`semantic-restore`, the one entry the facade cannot rewrite) reads it through the receiver's own cursor entry. No fixed-key route exists to misroute or strand anything; both P1s are structurally impossible.\n\n**Tests** (test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc):\n- `a-retained-ffi-request-migrates-and-the-retry-resumes` (:507-616): the two-call program now needs NO manual handoff — the re-point is deleted. New assertions: the lowered wait-side shape (`:stream-id vm/call-in-stream-key`; no `vm/call-in-stream-key`/`vm/call-out-stream-key`/`vm/call-out-cursor-key` in the lowered table, :571-577; the route cell at `:yin.k/c-0` naming the emitter's call-out reflection, :578-585); the retried request lands verbatim on the receiver's own call-in (:594-597); the migrated call resumes and the new call parks on the same pair (:598-601); nothing crossed to the emitter's pair (:602-610); the program halts with \"world!\" and an empty wait-set (:611-616).\n- `ffi-retained-round-trips` (:915-949): same shape assertions over stubs — fixed call-in key on the entry, pair never lowered, no fixed-cursor installation, route cell as its own fresh entry naming the emitter's reflection.\n- Confirmed behavior preserved: real parked shapes (`parked-requirer`/`parked-caller` unchanged), codec portability, frame-level cell sharing, the seven variants, and the r2 link fix (`a-lowered-link-request-retries-and-resumes-through-the-engine`, :449, untouched).\n\n**Lane counts (focused, exact).**\n- JVM `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.ucf.remote-test`: Ran 18 tests containing 163 assertions — 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- Node (shadow-cljs build; `node target/node-tests.js --test=yin.vm.ucf.remote-test`): Ran 18 tests containing 163 assertions — 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- Dart (`flutter test test/cljd-out/yin/vm/ucf/remote-test_test.dart` on the freshly `cljd`-compiled file): 18 of 18 passed — \"All tests passed!\".\n- Attribution: full-suite runs — the cljd suite's 127+ loading failures are demo/embed files and the shared cljd-out tree in-flight noise from the concurrent slice-5 work (0 of them in `yin.vm.ucf.remote-test`: 18 lines run, 0 in the failing list); the earlier Node full build's failures were all `dao.stream.ws.node-test` (slice-5 ws/rpc).\n- Hygiene: cljstyle check clean, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings, pure ASCII, ≤ 80 columns, no diagnostics; both slice-8 files remain the only ones I touched (untracked, no git operations).\n\nStatus: COMPLETE","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
