{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 22:30:59 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-28 05:30:59 ICT\n\n**The current tree does not pass the slice 8 gate.** I reviewed the files read-only and did not rerun the suites.\n\n- **P1 — Retained calls still use the emitter’s route.** The lower assigns a fresh reflection key to `:stream-id` and carries `:response-cursor` and `:response-stream` on the entry ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:625)). `semantic-restore` then makes the response wait use that carried route ([semantic.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:155)). This is not the reported receiver-local retry and response path. The test still asserts that the entry uses the receiver’s fixed call-in key ([remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:568)).\n- **P1 — Separate lowerings can reuse resource keys.** `fresh-key` checks only the supplied `used` set ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:485)). `lower-pending` defaults `occupied` to `nil` ([remote.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:739)), so separate calls can allocate the same `:yin.k/k-*` keys. In-batch sharing is preserved, but the former cross-frame collision is not structurally impossible.\n- **P1 — The retained-call test has an arity error.** `calling-machine` takes three arguments ([remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:288)); the test calls it with two ([remote_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc:529)). The supplied green results therefore cannot verify this exact current test file.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIED"}}
